# Kotlin Android Standards

- Use Kotlin idioms: data classes, sealed types, extension functions over Java patterns
{{#if parameters.useCompose}}
- Build UI with Jetpack Compose; hoist state and keep composables stateless where possible
- Use `remember` / `derivedStateOf` appropriately; avoid heavy work in composition
{{/if}}
{{#if parameters.mvvm}}
- ViewModels expose `StateFlow`/`UiState`; Activities/Fragments/Composables observe only
- No Android framework types in domain layer
{{/if}}
{{#if parameters.coroutines}}
- Use coroutines + Flow for async; inject dispatchers for testability
- Handle cancellation in long-running work
{{/if}}
- Dependency injection via Hilt; constructor injection for ViewModels and repositories
- Write instrumented tests for navigation; unit test ViewModels and use cases
